    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48460" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tmărŏs</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> , i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mountain in
			Epirus</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 8, 44</span></i>.—Called also
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tŏ-mărus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 2, 3,
				§ 6</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tmă-rĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Tmaros</i>, <i>Tmarian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Juppiter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. B. Get. 18</span></i>
			.</div>
